<title>USA: Baird group lifts American Precision stake.</title>
<headline>Baird group lifts American Precision stake.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by the Baird family of Buffalo, N.Y., said Friday it raised its stake in American Precision Industries Inc to 8.111 percent or 584,500 common shares.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the gorup said it bought 56,700 additional shares between July 23 and Sept 5 at prices ranging from $11.50 to $12.75 a share.</p>
<p>The group includes First Carolina Investors Inc, Cameron Baird Foundation and Aries Hill Corp.</p>
